{
  "dom_id": "step-q214479",
  "name": "Question 18",
  "problem": "Select the correct options in the statements below regarding residue classes modulo $12:$\n\n1. $[0]_{12}\\cap [6]_{12}=$ {{field-1}}\n\n2. $Z=$ \n{{field-2}}\n\n2. ${Z}_{12}=$ \n{{field-3}}",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the residue classes modulo $n$ have the following properties:\n\n- There are exactly $n$ distinct residue classes modulo $n$\n\n- Two distinct residue classes have an empty intersection: $[a]_{n}\\cap [b]_{n}=∅$ if $a≢b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)$\n\n- Residue classes modulo $n$ form a partition of the set of all integers: \n\n$$\nZ=[0]_{n}\\cup [1]_{n}\\cup ⋯\\cup [n-1]_{n}\n$$\n\n- The integers modulo $n$ is defined as the set containing all distinct residue classes modulo $n$: \n\n$$\n{Z}_{n}={[0]_{n},\\,[1]_{n},\\,…,\\,[n-1]_{n}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following properties:\n\n- $[0]_{12}\\cap [6]_{12}=∅.$\n\n- $Z=[0]_{12}\\cup [1]_{12}\\cup ⋯\\cup [11]_{12}.$\n\n- ${Z}_{12}={[0]_{12},[1]_{12},⋯,[11]_{12}}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
